WEBVTT

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:11.470
After the tragedy of the second duel, 
we're in anticipation for the third duel!

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:13.940
The resurrected grim reaper?

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:18.650
Those who dueled him have never 
dueled again due to fear.

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:22.290
That's why the strange D-Wheeler is famous.

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.140
Are you going to use that card?

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:35.770
I won't use Stardust.

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:39.620
I'm going to use Stardust when I 
have to settle things with Jack.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:06.390
No matter how far apart we 
are, we can't be stopped

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:11.390
That's deeply engraved into us

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:19.930
So don't be afraid of getting hurt

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:25.920
Break through even further

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:31.410
While carrying you beliefs in your heart

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:38.540
There's always only one truth

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:42.430
So feel the voice of your heart

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:47.190
With your unwavering emotions

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:53.320
Seize the signs of tomorrow

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:28.730
Flame RevengerSpeed King Skull Flame

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:41.110
King, I'm the one who's going to defeat you.

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:43.980
Here I go!

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:45.890
Who's that?  Stop!

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:47.460
Stop!

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:56.980
After him!

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:01.650
Hurry!  He went that way!

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:16.860
Do you understand?  In order to acquire data, you 
must hurt him as much as possible during the duel.

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:21.490
But don't let your guard down.  
He's the man who defeated the King.

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:23.560
The man who defeated the King?

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:30.050
A rat.

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:33.160
It was male.

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:38.050
The man who defeated the King.

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:46.000
Yusei is up next.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.560
I wonder if he'll be okay.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.040
There's no way Bro will lose!

00:03:57.190 --> 00:04:02.960
Everybody listen!  This is what you've 
all been waiting for!  A Riding Duel!

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:13.750
The first D-Wheeler selected to participate 
in the Fortune Cup is Yusei Fudo!

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:26.380
We don't want punks with markers!

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:27.730
Stop acting cool!

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:30.230
You can do it, Yusei!

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:41.180
His opponent D-Wheeler is Shira, 
the resurrected grim reaper!

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:51.710
We're counting on you, grim reaper!  
Don't lose to a guy with a marker!

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:53.300
Smash him!

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:57.110
Everyone's mean.  They don't 
have to hate him that much.

00:04:57.110 --> 00:05:00.350
Now come!

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:08.180
It's finally time for the duel!

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:13.060
Set on the Field Spell Speed World!

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:16.490
Duel mode on.  Autopilot standby.

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:21.160
Speed World has taken over the field!

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:25.100
Now spells that aren't Speed 
Spells can't be activated!

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:33.260
There's the start signal of 
destiny with the countdown!

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:37.460
It's time for the Riding Duel!  Acceleration!

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:46.760
Sorry to keep you waiting!  
Mukuro Enjo has arrived!

00:05:46.760 --> 00:05:49.480
This is a surprise!

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:53.390
Underneath the hood is the 
fiery D-Wheeler who's willing

00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:56.890
to risk his life to defeat 
the King!  Mukuro Enjo!!

00:05:56.890 --> 00:05:58.380
What's the meaning of this?

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:01.840
Director, Shira is out of commission.

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:06.700
The flaming ghost…

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:14.600
I'm your opponent.  I'll show you 
what a Riding Duel is really about!

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:17.310
What's wrong, Yusei?

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:22.090
If you're also a D-Wheeler, then 
accept Mukuro Enjo's challenge!

00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:25.150
Fine.

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:27.410
I'll be your opponent!

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:31.210
This is...  Umm…

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:34.240
This will be entertaining.

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:39.290
The organizer has given permission!

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:41.870
The duel continues!

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:46.100
I go first!

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:50.700
I draw!  From my hand, I 
summon Burning Skullhead!

00:06:50.990 --> 00:06:54.500
I set three cards and end my turn!

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:55.770
My turn.

00:06:58.090 --> 00:07:00.160
I summon Speed Warrior!

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:08.770
Yusei has immediately gone on the offensive!

00:07:08.770 --> 00:07:12.450
Due to Speed Warrior's monster effect, 
its attack points are doubled

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:15.550
during the Battle Phase of the 
turn in which it was summoned!

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:16.460
Battle!

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:19.300
There goes Speed Warrior!

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:22.440
I activate the trap Zero Guard!

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:26.320
By making the attack points of 
one monster on my field equal 0,

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:29.320
it cannot be destroyed in battle this turn!

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:30.940
Sonic Edge!

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:40.250
Mukuro Enjo has already 
taken 1800 points of damage!

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:42.510
What's he doing?

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:45.510
In order to protect his monster, 
he gave up his life points.

00:07:45.510 --> 00:07:51.070
And if he took 1800 points of damage at 
once, then his Speed Counters will be…

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:52.420
They haven't decreased!

00:07:52.420 --> 00:07:55.240
I activate the trap Doom Accelerator!

00:07:55.240 --> 00:08:02.310
When I take battle damage, I gain one Speed 
Counter for every 500 points of damage!

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:06.830
He gained three Speed Counters!

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:08.880
See that?

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:14.060
Mukuro Enjo has created the 
invincible Speed Acceleration Deck!

00:08:14.270 --> 00:08:17.250
Well done, Mukuro!  Beat him up!

00:08:17.250 --> 00:08:19.020
So you're challenging me with Speed Spells.

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:21.590
I accept and face that challenge!

00:08:21.590 --> 00:08:24.220
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:08:25.490 --> 00:08:27.140
My turn.

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:28.630
I draw!

00:08:28.630 --> 00:08:31.980
I activate the Speed Spell Summon Speeder!

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:35.060
When I have four or more Speed Counters,

00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:38.760
I can Special Summon one Level 
4-or-below monster from my hand!

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:40.540
Come, Skull Base!

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:46.920
By releasing Skull Base and Burning 
Skullhead, I can Advance Summon Skull Flame!

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:55.820
When Skull Base is released in order to 
Advance Summon, I get to draw one card.

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:56.990
Battle!

00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:06.480
Mukuro Enjo!

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:13.130
By using a Speed Spell for a splendid 
combination attack, he equalized their life points!

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:14.880
Well done, Mukuro!

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:19.430
I'm only getting started.  
Watch this and be shocked!

00:09:19.430 --> 00:09:23.230
I activate the Continuous Trap Speed Booster!

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:27.330
What's that?

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:31.050
This is the true potential of 
the Speed Acceleration Deck!

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:34.580
I'm only getting started, Yusei.

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:51.760
This is the true potential of 
the Speed Acceleration Deck!

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:57.550
I can activate the Continuous Trap Speed 
Booster when I have more Speed Counters than you!

00:09:57.550 --> 00:10:00.050
During your turn, I can negate 
your monsters' attacks

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:02.890
the same number of times as the 
difference in our Speed Counters.

00:10:02.890 --> 00:10:05.410
Also, once during each of my turns,

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:09.410
I can deal damage equal to the difference 
in our Speed Counters multiplied by 100!

00:10:09.410 --> 00:10:10.900
What does that mean?

00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:16.560
The greater the difference in their Speed 
Counters, the more Mukuro has the advantage.

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:20.170
Yusei looks like he's having fun.

00:10:20.170 --> 00:10:24.260
But isn't he in a bad situation?  Why 
does he look like he's having fun?

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:31.350
Stop laughing!  I activate 
Speed Booster's effect!

00:10:37.820 --> 00:10:40.250
With that attack, he's gained 
the advantage in life points!

00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:42.680
Mukuro has more life points!

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:46.410
No one can keep up with my speed!

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:49.840
I set one card and end my turn.

00:10:50.590 --> 00:10:54.330
How's that?  No matter how fast you're 
driving, you can't see me anymore.

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:55.690
What?

00:10:55.690 --> 00:10:56.620
I draw.

00:10:56.620 --> 00:10:59.350
How can you keep up when you 
only have 1 Speed Counter?

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:03.240
Slip Stream!

00:11:03.770 --> 00:11:05.470
Slip Stream?

00:11:05.470 --> 00:11:06.770
That's right.

00:11:06.770 --> 00:11:10.240
You can activate that trap when 
you have less Speed Counters

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:13.140
than your opponent, and your 
opponent uses a Speed Spell.

00:11:13.540 --> 00:11:16.920
During the next Standby Phase, 
you can have the same number

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:18.920
of Speed Counters as your opponent.

00:11:19.880 --> 00:11:21.020
Nicely done.

00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:23.230
When did he activate that trap?

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:26.390
I see.  You activated it back then!

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:30.140
I activate the Speed Spell Summon Speeder!

00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:32.290
I activate my trap.

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:33.810
Slip Stream.

00:11:35.830 --> 00:11:41.040
This is fun, Yusei!  However, 
can you keep up with my speed?

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:43.800
I activate the trap Acceleration Zone!

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:46.460
Here I go!

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:57.340
What speed!

00:11:57.630 --> 00:12:00.900
His Speed Counters are up to eleven!

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:09.260
With Acceleration Zone, if you gain 
Speed Counters using a method different

00:12:09.260 --> 00:12:13.160
than Speed World's effect, 
I gain five Speed Counters!

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:16.130
You can't keep up with this speed!

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:21.710
I activate the Speed Spell Summon Speeder!

00:12:23.390 --> 00:12:26.760
Yusei is countering with Summon Speeder!

00:12:28.090 --> 00:12:32.010
Due to the effect of Summon Speeder, 
I Special Summon Quillbolt Hedgehog.

00:12:32.010 --> 00:12:35.110
Then I Normal Summon Junk Synchron.

00:12:35.510 --> 00:12:38.220
Due to Junk Synchron's monster effect,

00:12:38.220 --> 00:12:41.220
I get to Special Summon Speed 
Warrior from my graveyard.

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:44.040
Come, Speed Warrior!

00:12:47.980 --> 00:12:52.390
Level 3 Junk Synchron tunes 
Level 2 Speed Warrior.

00:12:55.820 --> 00:13:01.190
The stars come together to call forth a new 
power!  Become the path that lights the way!

00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:04.190
Synchro Summon!

00:13:05.040 --> 00:13:07.570
Come, Junk Warrior!

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:14.510
He did it!

00:13:14.510 --> 00:13:17.030
That's Bro's card.

00:13:17.510 --> 00:13:20.990
Junk Warrior gains attack points 
equal to the attack points

00:13:20.990 --> 00:13:23.790
of Level 2-or-below monsters on the field.

00:13:23.790 --> 00:13:24.930
Battle!

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:28.860
I activate the effect of Speed Booster!

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:36.650
Junk Warrior's attack doesn't work!

00:13:36.650 --> 00:13:39.750
With Speed Booster, he can negate 
attacks the same number of times

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:42.310
as the difference in their Speed Counters.

00:13:42.310 --> 00:13:49.760
Since Mukuro has eleven and Yusei 
has six, he can negate five attacks?

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:52.310
All I can do for now is survive.

00:13:53.030 --> 00:13:55.710
I set one card and end my turn.

00:13:57.150 --> 00:13:59.430
My turn.  I draw!

00:14:00.280 --> 00:14:02.470
There it is!

00:14:02.470 --> 00:14:06.660
12 Speed Counters!  That's the maximum speed!

00:14:07.170 --> 00:14:11.770
That's right!  The person who rules 
speed also rules the Riding Duel!

00:14:11.770 --> 00:14:17.430
This speed will lead to the King!  That's 
what I believed while I was training!

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:23.280
In order to reach the speed of the King!

00:14:25.990 --> 00:14:30.670
I'll finish you in an instant!  I activate 
the Speed Spell Accelerate Draw!

00:14:30.670 --> 00:14:33.330
Due to its effect, I draw two cards!

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:37.230
I drew it!

00:14:37.530 --> 00:14:40.580
The Speed Spell End of the Storm!

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:41.330
What?

00:14:41.330 --> 00:14:42.870
End of the Storm?

00:14:43.140 --> 00:14:45.080
This is the King's card.

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:51.380
I'll show you how a King battles 
using End of the Storm!

00:14:51.380 --> 00:14:54.590
I activate End of the Storm!

00:14:57.010 --> 00:15:01.290
I can activate End of the Storm when 
I have ten or more Speed Counters.

00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:04.060
All monsters on our fields are destroyed,

00:15:04.060 --> 00:15:07.860
and we take 300 points of damage 
for each destroyed monster!

00:15:12.780 --> 00:15:16.790
Yusei's life points have 
immediately dropped to 1300!

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:22.050
However, Mukuro destroyed his 
own monster, so he can't attack!

00:15:22.050 --> 00:15:23.650
What's he going to do?

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:25.910
It's all within my calculations.

00:15:25.910 --> 00:15:29.980
I remove one Skull Flame 
in my graveyard from play!

00:15:30.430 --> 00:15:33.750
By doing this, I can Special 
Summon a special monster!

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:37.470
C'mon, Speed King Skull Flame!

00:15:42.740 --> 00:15:43.450
What?

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:45.100
3000 attack points?

00:15:45.100 --> 00:15:50.010
Not only did he destroy all monsters 
on the field and deal damage,

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:54.010
but it led to the summoning 
of a high level monster!

00:15:54.010 --> 00:15:56.050
What a perfect combo!

00:15:57.410 --> 00:16:00.090
The Speed Acceleration Deck 
is something to be feared!

00:16:01.450 --> 00:16:03.130
This will end it all!

00:16:03.130 --> 00:16:07.590
Speed King Skull Flame, 
attack Yusei directly!

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:11.610
I activate my trap!

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:13.250
Scrap-Iron Scarecrow.

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:17.610
Yusei avoided it with a trap!

00:16:17.610 --> 00:16:20.910
Then I activate the effect of Speed Booster!

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:30.690
Yusei!

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:35.070
With Speed King Skull Flame's monster effect,

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:39.570
you take 400 points of damage for every 
Burning Skullhead in my graveyard!

00:16:45.610 --> 00:16:49.730
Now Yusei only has 400 life points remaining!

00:16:49.730 --> 00:16:53.710
Stardust.  Use Stardust.

00:16:54.940 --> 00:16:57.650
This is a great turn of events.

00:17:00.090 --> 00:17:01.420
My turn!

00:17:03.150 --> 00:17:06.630
I activate the Speed Spell Shift Down!

00:17:08.950 --> 00:17:12.400
Yusei intentionally decreased 
his own Speed Counters!

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:14.550
What's the meaning of this?

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:17.080
He's betting on potential.

00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:18.570
Potential?

00:17:18.570 --> 00:17:19.550
Yes.

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:24.070
The Speed Spell Shift Down decreases 
his Speed Counters by six,

00:17:24.070 --> 00:17:26.970
but he can now draw two cards from his deck.

00:17:26.970 --> 00:17:30.190
I see.  His heart believes in his cards.

00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:30.980
Yeah.

00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:33.880
That's his strength.

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:40.740
Due to the effect of Shift 
Down, I draw two cards.

00:17:40.930 --> 00:17:43.030
I summon Nitro Synchron.

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:50.710
When I have a Tuner Monster, I can Special 
Summon Quillbolt Hedgehog from my graveyard.

00:17:53.500 --> 00:17:57.300
Then I activate the trap card Give & Take.

00:17:57.300 --> 00:18:03.070
With this, I can Special Summon a monster in 
my graveyard to your field in defense position.

00:18:03.070 --> 00:18:04.030
What?

00:18:05.590 --> 00:18:09.290
Then one monster on my 
field gains Levels equal

00:18:09.290 --> 00:18:12.290
to the Level of the monster 
that was Special Summoned.

00:18:12.830 --> 00:18:17.050
Quillbolt Hedgehog is now Level 5.  
And with Level 2 Nitro Synchron…

00:18:17.050 --> 00:18:19.740
He can Synchro Summon a Level 7 monster!

00:18:20.270 --> 00:18:23.620
Nitro Synchron tunes Quillbolt Hedgehog!

00:18:23.810 --> 00:18:29.250
Our thoughts combine to call forth a new 
power!  Become the path that lights the way!

00:18:30.320 --> 00:18:31.810
Synchro Summon!

00:18:31.810 --> 00:18:34.410
Burn up, Nitro Warrior!

00:18:35.660 --> 00:18:41.800
That was pointless!  As long as I have 
Speed Booster, you can't attack me!

00:18:43.820 --> 00:18:49.430
But when Nitro Warrior is Synchro Summoned, 
he can draw one card from his deck.

00:18:49.430 --> 00:18:51.420
Is that what Yusei was aiming for?

00:18:51.420 --> 00:18:52.590
That's right.

00:18:52.590 --> 00:18:54.670
It all depends on the next card.

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:57.350
Yusei.

00:18:57.750 --> 00:19:01.230
I'll overtake you with my speed!

00:19:17.160 --> 00:19:18.060
It's here.

00:19:18.650 --> 00:19:21.680
I activate the Speed Spell Gap Storm!

00:19:23.110 --> 00:19:24.570
What?

00:19:24.570 --> 00:19:29.040
I can activate Gap Storm when the difference 
in our Speed Counters is ten or more.

00:19:29.460 --> 00:19:33.000
All spell and trap cards 
on the field are destroyed.

00:19:33.530 --> 00:19:35.020
That means…

00:19:35.020 --> 00:19:38.180
That includes my Speed Booster!

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:41.560
I see!  Yusei was waiting for that card!

00:19:41.560 --> 00:19:44.670
That's why he decreased 
his own Speed Counters!

00:19:45.650 --> 00:19:46.720
Damn.

00:19:47.090 --> 00:19:49.030
Yusei.

00:19:49.030 --> 00:19:51.340
Next, my monster effect.

00:19:51.340 --> 00:19:57.910
When I activate a spell card on my own turn, 
Nitro Warrior gains 1000 attack points.

00:19:57.910 --> 00:19:59.240
What?

00:19:59.240 --> 00:20:00.270
Battle!

00:20:02.690 --> 00:20:05.620
Go, Nitro Warrior!

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:08.300
Dynamite Knuckle!

00:20:15.030 --> 00:20:16.200
Damn!

00:20:17.370 --> 00:20:20.180
When Nitro Warrior destroys your monster,

00:20:20.180 --> 00:20:24.380
one monster on your field in defense 
position switches to attack position,

00:20:24.380 --> 00:20:26.380
and Nitro Warrior can attack it.

00:20:26.380 --> 00:20:31.510
What?  Attack position?  Then 
that means Junk Synchron wll…

00:20:32.950 --> 00:20:33.720
Battle!

00:20:34.780 --> 00:20:38.020
The difference in their 
attack points is huge!

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:42.380
Oh no!

00:20:45.440 --> 00:20:47.270
It's over!

00:20:47.940 --> 00:20:51.790
With an excellent combo, Yusei 
has a come-from-behind victory!

00:20:52.330 --> 00:20:54.560
He did it!  Yusei won!

00:20:54.560 --> 00:20:56.500
Bro, you're incredible!

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:06.650
It was a good duel.

00:21:06.650 --> 00:21:12.580
Yeah.  I lost today, but 
I won't lose next time.

00:21:25.100 --> 00:21:27.810
Like I thought, he wasn't strong enough.

00:21:28.270 --> 00:21:30.500
That means the next will be…

00:21:34.010 --> 00:21:37.840
What have you been planning this entire time?

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:09.630
What can we grasp?  What can we do?

00:22:09.990 --> 00:22:15.020
We'll step forward and find out

00:22:15.400 --> 00:22:20.950
My unstoppable emotions, the 
beating of my passionate heart

00:22:21.100 --> 00:22:26.180
I heard the voice of truth

00:22:26.370 --> 00:22:29.340
After I was hurt, I learned

00:22:31.910 --> 00:22:34.930
Of a place where I can become stronger

00:22:36.880 --> 00:22:42.090
I stack my dreams in my palm

00:22:42.220 --> 00:22:47.490
And I'll someday pass them to you

00:22:47.920 --> 00:22:53.430
Seeking for the signal 
to start, my soul roars

00:22:53.730 --> 00:22:58.770
I will overcome my suffocating 
and mediocre life

00:22:59.310 --> 00:23:04.840
I'll dash and acquire all the bright futures

00:23:04.980 --> 00:23:14.250
Carrying the bonds I believe 
in, I run towards tomorrow
